#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# asymptotic_sum

#% text
# `asymptotic_sum(f, [k, a, b], [x, x0, m])` gives the expansion of the sum of f over k to order m in x at x0; `x -> x0` gives the leading term.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For a parameter x at a finite point the summand is expanded and summed term by term; otherwise the closed-form sum is expanded.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
asymptotic_sum(1/(k^2 + a), [k, 1, inf], [a, 0, 2])
#% output
#= (1/6)*pi^2 - (1/90)*a*pi^4 + (1/945)*a^2*pi^6

#% cell
asymptotic_sum(1/(k^2 - 1), [k, 2, n], [n, inf, 3])
#% output
#= 3/4 - n^-1 - 1/(2*n^3) + 1/(2*n^2)

#% cell
asymptotic_sum(1/(k^3 + a), [k, 1, inf], [a, 0, 1])
#% output
#= (-1/945)*a*pi^6 + zeta(3)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `sum`, `series`, `asymptotic_product`, `asymptotic_integrate`
